Third-party and shared ArtCraft material

This repository links:
- `craft-proof`, `craft-atomic`, `craft-docx`, `craft-wordmodel`, and `craft` (`ui`, `ui-app`,
  `theme-store`, `dialogs`, and dev `ui-testing`) from `storytold/craft-libs` at revision
  `8be80b006888ae023d61eed265241c9b78b84981` (MIT OR Apache-2.0);
- `craft-ai-core`, `craft-ai-openai`, and `craft-ai-client` from `storytold/craft-ai-integrations`
  at revision `a822ad5b4db2c0dcd7a43bb62d6d75251fd3f8b5` (MIT OR Apache-2.0);
- Craft's `storytold/egui` fork (`932a73b28560acb1a695533307b2cd0d66a42081`, MIT OR Apache-2.0) and
  `storytold/winit` fork (`a517b3846ee8457d84ee4975110bfda6797c44dc`, Apache-2.0).

`craft-proof` bundles the following non-code word lists and (when built with `CRAFT_I18N_DIR` set)
build-time language data recorded in `storytold/craft-libs`'s `NOTICE` and `ATTRIBUTION.md`:

- `crates/proof/data/en-words.dic`: public domain, the words of the Moby Hyphenator II list by
  Grady Ward (Project Gutenberg eBook #3204), without its break points.
- `crates/proof/data/en-extra.txt`: MIT OR Apache-2.0, WordCraft contributors' list of modern
  English words (from `storytold/craft-i18n` `language-data/en-us/en-extra.txt`).
- Optional build-time `CRAFT_I18N_DIR` language data: when enabled for release builds, each embedded
  file keeps its upstream notice from `storytold/craft-i18n` and `storytold/craft-libs` (including
  the BSD-3-Clause notice for Portuguese hyphenation patterns `language-data/pt/hyphenation.pat`,
  Copyright (C) 1987, 1994, 1996, 2015 Pedro J. de Rezende, 1996, 2015 J. Joao Dias Almeida,
  2024 Leonardo Araujo and Aline Benevides, and SCOWL notices where embedded).

Every other dependency is a crates.io package whose licence is listed in its own manifest; keep new
dependencies inside the suite's licence allowlist (`storytold/craft-contrib` `standards/licences.md`)
and record any non-code asset in `ATTRIBUTION.md` in the same change.
